## Implementation checkpoint — 2026-10-08

Normal import is `uv run python scripts/corpus_rel_policy.py --input <approved-policy-scope-manifest.json> --output <rel_policy_dispositions.csv> --scope full_facets|discipline_only --archive-root <parent-run-root> --pool <pool.csv> --table <icf_screen.csv> --dimensions <rel_dimensions.csv> --run-id <stable-id> --labelled-at <stable-date>`. The versioned config registers the immutable approved manifest. It verifies the pool, both disjoint rosters, scientific decision, exact proof gaps, calibration failure and separate native attempt hashes before constructing policy rows. The compatibility prompt_sha256 field carries the deterministic policy method hash; no prompt, native answer or model-assessed quality is invented.

A separate append-only policy table binds each canonical policy row to its exact source and scientific authority. Full-facet scope appends ICF unsure and dimensions; dimension-only appends catchup dimensions and no ICF/facet row. Views activate restriction from selected policy provenance and clear it when a later valid assessment is selected. Native facet counts and policy counts are separate.

Scientific clarification: included selected-policy rows are bibliometric_only/local_screen_abstention. Excluded rows preserve rel_use empty, their exclusion reason and membership, while exposing local_screen_abstention=true and the exact selected policy restriction/provenance. Nonempty source abstracts are preserved and abstract_flag remains the existing raw-empty predicate. This supersedes the earlier blanket wording “all policy rows are bibliometric_only”.

